---
import UtilityLayout from "../layouts/UtilityLayout.astro";
import tools from "../data/tools.json";
---

<UtilityLayout
  title="Free data, text and planning tools"
  description="UtilityPot combines Jev interpretation with reviewed, deterministic utilities for CSV, JSON, dates, meetings, entities, diagrams and webpage evidence."
  slug=""
  overview
>
  <div class="product-hero">
    <section class="hero-copy">
      <p class="coordinate">OPEN-SOURCE UTILITIES / PART OF MODEPOT</p>
      <h1>
        Useful tools.
        <br />
        Inspectable results.
      </h1>
      <p class="utility-intro">
        Map messy data, plan across time zones, extract entities or sketch a
        flowchart. Jev interprets what you mean; you review the proposal; code
        performs the exact work.
      </p>
      <div class="hero-actions">
        <a class="primary" href="#tools">
          Browse tools →
        </a>
        <a class="secondary" href="#how-it-works">
          How it works
        </a>
        <a href="https://github.com/tugrulguner/utilitypot">GitHub</a>
      </div>
      <p class="creator-credit">
        Created by <a href="https://tugrul.modepot.io/">Tugrul Guner</a> · Part
        of <a href="https://modepot.io/">ModePot</a>
      </p>
    </section>
    <img
      class="product-art"
      src="/utilitypot-lockup-v1.png"
      alt="UtilityPot: Jev interprets. You review. Code executes. Part of ModePot."
      width="1200"
      height="900"
      fetchpriority="high"
    />
  </div>
  <section id="tools" class="tools-section">
    <p class="coordinate">CHOOSE A TASK</p>
    <h2>Seven tools. No signup.</h2>
    <div class="tool-cards">
      {tools.map(({ slug, title, description }) => (
        <article class="panel">
          <h3>{title}</h3>
          <p class="notice">{description}</p>
          <a
            class="tool-link"
            aria-label={`Open ${title}`}
            href={`/tools/${slug}/`}
          >
            Open {title} →
          </a>
        </article>
      ))}
    </div>
  </section>
  <section id="how-it-works" class="prose">
    <p class="coordinate">HOW THE TOOLS WORK</p>
    <h2>Interpret. Review. Run.</h2>
    <p>
      Jev selects bounded interpretations and source evidence. You review
      mappings, time windows, entities or graph structure. Deterministic code
      then transforms data, computes times, checks exact source spans or renders
      the diagram.
    </p>
    <ol class="mechanism-steps">
      <li>
        <strong>Interpret meaning.</strong> Send limited context only after
        explicit consent.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Review the proposal.</strong> Inspect the selected settings and
        uncertainty before using them.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Run exact operations.</strong> Preview and download the result;
        no arbitrary generated code is executed.
      </li>
    </ol>
    <p>
      Ordinary conversion, date cleanup, scheduling and manual diagram rendering
      run locally without an AI call. AI success is not a correctness guarantee;
      entity extraction is bounded, Mermaid output is limited to reviewed
      flowcharts, and webpage answers are source excerpts rather than generated
      essays.
    </p>
    <p>
      No account or saved input history. Submitted AI context is processed by
      TypeSafe. <a href="/privacy/">Read privacy and operating limits</a> or{" "}
      <a href="https://github.com/tugrulguner/utilitypot#local-setup">
        run UtilityPot locally
      </a>
      .
    </p>
  </section>
</UtilityLayout>
